{"nodes": [{"id": "plan_expenses", "label": "Expense Tracking Plan", "file_type": "document", "source_file": "PLAN-EXPENSES.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Phase 1c. Workflow settled 2026-09-13 and 2026-09-14. One capability file; core untouched. All five steps shipped, with two marked departures."}, {"id": "migrations_003_expenses_schema", "label": "003_expenses.sql", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "PLAN-EXPENSES.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "expenses table plus users.cards. Shipped with Phase 1b because card-bill payments needed a place to land."}, {"id": "plan_expenses_e1_extract_on_arrival", "label": "E1 Extract on Arrival", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "PLAN-EXPENSES.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "The extract-on-arrival versus park-until-digest trade assumed extraction was a model call. Phase 1b showed the emails are a fixed template family, so regex runs on arrival, status pending carries the question, and nothing raw is stored."}, {"id": "plan_expenses_e2_asymmetric_dedupe", "label": "E2 Asymmetric Dedupe", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "PLAN-EXPENSES.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "An email that matches a chat row of the same amount in the last 60 minutes is discarded. A later chat entry attaches to a pending row of the same amount on the same day, unless two pending rows match, in which case neither is chosen. Every spend has one row: the bank supplies the amount and the user supplies the meaning."}, {"id": "plan_expenses_e3_digest_in_code", "label": "E3 Digest Composed in Code", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "PLAN-EXPENSES.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Listing rows and quoting amounts is not a judgement. A model should not do subtraction on money, the same reason A6 keeps budget arithmetic in code. The model is used only when the user replies."}, {"id": "plan_expenses_e4_one_digest", "label": "E4 One Message a Day", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "PLAN-EXPENSES.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "No immediate spend alerts. The planning nag exists because an assistant that interrupts twice stops being read. With budgets out of scope the digest reports and asks."}, {"id": "plan_expenses_e5_no_sms", "label": "E5 No SMS", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "PLAN-EXPENSES.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "SMS would need a forwarder with read access to every message, including OTPs, to buy latency a 21:00 digest does not need. Cash stays fully manual. Anything the bank only texts is never captured."}, {"id": "plan_expenses_e6_splits_chat_only", "label": "E6 Splits Are Chat Only", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "PLAN-EXPENSES.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "A bank email cannot know a dinner was split. Buttons cannot carry an amount under the D11 payload and label caps, so there is no split button."}, {"id": "plan_expenses_e7_kind", "label": "E7 kind Is Highest Risk", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "PLAN-EXPENSES.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Reading a card-bill payment as a spend double-counts the month, silently. kind gets its own labelled set before the capability is trusted."}, {"id": "plan_expenses_e8_cards_config", "label": "E8 Cards Are Config", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "PLAN-EXPENSES.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "users.cards is the single source of truth: match strings, credit or debit or cash, and statement close day. No stored aggregate, because five write paths would drift and a wrong total looks authoritative. expenses.card is validated against the keys at write time so adding a card is not a migration. On a cc_payment row, card is the card being paid."}, {"id": "plan_expenses_e9_bill_is_a_bound", "label": "E9 Bill Is a Bound", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "PLAN-EXPENSES.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "The statement does not match captured spend exactly. Posting lag, auth versus settlement, un-alerted fees, refunds, and reversed authorisations are systematic gaps. A stable small delta is noise; a growing delta means alerts are not firing. This outside check exists only for the four credit cards."}, {"id": "plan_expenses_categories", "label": "Expense Categories", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "PLAN-EXPENSES.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Eleven values enforced by a CHECK: food, groceries, transport, housing, subscriptions, shopping, health, travel, entertainment, fees, other. food and groceries move independently. housing includes utilities. A card bill is not a category."}, {"id": "plan_expenses_cards", "label": "Card Configuration", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "PLAN-EXPENSES.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Seven values including cash: amex_everyday, discover, chase_freedom, apple_card, chase_debit, sofi_debit, cash. Credit versus debit matters only so debit or cash cannot be a cc_payment and so reconciliation covers the four credit cards."}, {"id": "plan_expenses_digest", "label": "Evening Digest", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "PLAN-EXPENSES.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "At users.digest_hour, default 21, guarded by last_digest_on. Composed in code. Shipped without buttons because Fix one cannot carry an answer. Skipped on an empty day."}, {"id": "plan_expenses_kind", "label": "Expense kind", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "PLAN-EXPENSES.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "spend, refund, transfer, or cc_payment. transfer and cc_payment are stored and excluded from every spending total. cc_payment is a settlement of swipes already counted."}, {"id": "plan_expenses_budgets_out", "label": "Budgets Out of Scope", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "PLAN-EXPENSES.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "No users.budgets column and no overspend line. Metrics come after the foundation. Reversing it is one jsonb column and one line in the digest composer."}, {"id": "plan_expenses_spent_at", "label": "spent_at From the Alert", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "PLAN-EXPENSES.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "The transaction time in the email, not poll time. Using now() puts spending on the wrong day and, four times a year, the wrong month. Same rule as local_today: one helper."}, {"id": "capabilities_expenses_log_expense", "label": "log_expense", "file_type": "code", "source_file": "PLAN-EXPENSES.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Chat write path. Runs the E2 attach rule before insert. Computes share and owed. Category and card are validated."}, {"id": "capabilities_expenses_update_expense", "label": "update_expense", "file_type": "code", "source_file": "PLAN-EXPENSES.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Recomputes share and owed when amount or headcount changes, and confirms a pending row. Never used for settlement."}, {"id": "capabilities_expenses_settle_split", "label": "settle_split", "file_type": "code", "source_file": "PLAN-EXPENSES.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Subtracts a repayment from owed_amount only. share_amount stays put so monthly spend does not climb when a friend pays you back."}, {"id": "capabilities_expenses_card_summary", "label": "card_summary", "file_type": "code", "source_file": "PLAN-EXPENSES.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "E9 for credit cards over a statement window. The delta is a signal, not an exact match."}, {"id": "capabilities_expenses_digest", "label": "digest", "file_type": "code", "source_file": "PLAN-EXPENSES.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Code-composed 21:00 report. Fired from the hourly cron and guarded so it cannot send twice."}, {"id": "capabilities_gmail_parse_is_spend", "label": "is_spend", "file_type": "code", "source_file": "PLAN-EXPENSES.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Lane C detector in gmail_parse.py. Deterministic replacement for the extract() model call the plan originally assumed."}, {"id": "capabilities_gmail_parse_parse_spend", "label": "parse_spend", "file_type": "code", "source_file": "PLAN-EXPENSES.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Extracts amount, merchant, spent_on, and card. Does not guess a category, because a guessed category would look like an answer."}, {"id": "capabilities_gmail_write_spend", "label": "_write_spend", "file_type": "code", "source_file": "PLAN-EXPENSES.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Inserts a pending spend. Discards the email when E2 finds a recent chat row of the same amount, and logs that discard."}, {"id": "core_db_recent_chat_expense", "label": "recent_chat_expense", "file_type": "code", "source_file": "PLAN-EXPENSES.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "E2 email direction: a chat row of the same amount in the last 60 minutes."}, {"id": "core_db_pending_match", "label": "pending_match", "file_type": "code", "source_file": "PLAN-EXPENSES.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "E2 chat direction: pending rows of the same amount on the same day. Replaces a single find_match whose source flag read backwards at both call sites."}, {"id": "core_db_expenses_between", "label": "expenses_between", "file_type": "code", "source_file": "PLAN-EXPENSES.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Range read for the digest and the breakdown. Index scan on expenses_month_idx."}, {"id": "core_db_pending_expenses", "label": "pending_expenses", "file_type": "code", "source_file": "PLAN-EXPENSES.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Rows the digest asks about. Amount already counts; meaning is still blank."}, {"id": "core_db_outstanding_owed", "label": "outstanding_owed", "file_type": "code", "source_file": "PLAN-EXPENSES.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Sum of positive owed_amount. Shown in the digest only when non-zero."}, {"id": "test_phase1_suite", "label": "test_phase1.py", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "PLAN-EXPENSES.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Offline checks for recurrence, expenses, the digest, and one end-to-end pass."}], "edges": [{"source": "plan_expenses", "target": "plan_v1", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "PLAN-EXPENSES.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "plan_expenses", "target": "evaluation_plan", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "PLAN-EXPENSES.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "plan_expenses", "target": "plan_expenses_e1_extract_on_arrival", "relation": "conceptually_related_to", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "PLAN-EXPENSES.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "plan_expenses", "target": "plan_expenses_e2_asymmetric_dedupe", "relation": "conceptually_related_to", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "PLAN-EXPENSES.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "plan_expenses", "target": "plan_expenses_e3_digest_in_code", "relation": "conceptually_related_to", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "PLAN-EXPENSES.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "plan_expenses", "target": "plan_expenses_e4_one_digest", "relation": "conceptually_related_to", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "PLAN-EXPENSES.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "plan_expenses", "target": "plan_expenses_e5_no_sms", "relation": "conceptually_related_to", "confidence": "EXTRACT